% BINN camera-ready bibliography
% Do not invent citations; prefer on-disk hashes in Methods.
%
% The ten SHD-literature entries below were read against their primary sources
% on 2026-09-03 and every field here -- volume, issue, pages, DOI, venue --
% comes from the arXiv API or Crossref rather than from recollection. The
% check, including the three claims it corrected, is
% results/CITATIONS_2026-09-03_SECTION_0_AGAINST_PRIMARIES.md, and
% scripts/check_section0_citations.py fails if this file and that record
% disagree about which sources exist.
%
% The entries above that line are the secondary program's. They carry venue and
% year only: no volume, pages or DOI has been added to them, because there is no
% network in this repository and a field that cannot be verified must not be
% filled in from recollection. They are stubs, and saying so is the point.
%
% 2026-09-10. Citations were wired up (`[key]` citations in the draft, pandoc --natbib),
% and rendering the bibliography for the first time exposed three things it had
% been hiding:
%   * `reinforce1992` carried raw `_` in a note and broke pdflatex outright.
%   * Five notes were maintainer instructions about THIS repository -- "BINN
%     Gate G2-style bars", protocol hashes -- and were being typeset into a
%     double-blind submission. They are `%` comments above their entries now:
%     still readable here, no longer printed there.
%   * `shd2019` was the arXiv preprint of `cramer2022`, the same dataset paper
%     under two keys, and `binn_results_freeze` pointed at two documents that
%     `build_results_index.describe` reports retired. Both are removed; neither
%     was cited, and neither is in the 2026-09-03 verification record.

